{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "process-evap-leaks-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.5 step 7d: the `process-evap-leaks` RunSpec computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE. It mounts `moves-onroad.esm` -- the 69 national tables and the onroad model -- and supplies the thirteen things that are this run's: year 2020, August, hour 7, weekday, source type 21, road type 4, its four source-fuel types, three pollutant-processes, an EMPTY chained-to relation and county 26161, plus the expected output.\n\nIT IS THE FIRST EVAPORATIVE RUN HERE, and the first to leave the exhaust processes entirely. The calculator is `LiquidLeakingCalculator`, a direct master-loop subscriber: activity, cohorts, a base rate read from a table, one multiplication. No temperature adjustment, no fuel adjustment, no humidity term, no A/C term, no speciation -- all four of those tables were measured and carry no row at `polProcessID` 113, so the factors this port already applies are their identities and the arm it adds is only the operating-mode weight.\n\nWHAT THE MODEL GAINED, and it is smaller than the family looks. MOVES weights a rated pollutant-process's operating modes with a `RatesOpModeDistribution` over speed bins; an evaporative one is written by a different generator entirely, over SOAKING and RUNNING. So `pp_W` acquired an alternative rather than a term: `evap_W`, E1's `fractionOfOperating` from the ratio of SHO to `SourceHours`, E2's soak weights and E3's residual on mode 300. Everything else was already here -- the activity chain, the source-bin distribution and its fuel-usage rebase, the age-group join into `emissionRateByAge`, and `SHO / noOfRealDays`, which is exactly the inventory calculator's activity.\n\nWHAT THE DEFAULT DATABASE DOES NOT HAVE, measured before a line was written. Six tables this run's execution database carried are absent or empty nationally. `sourceBin` and `sourceBinDistribution` are empty because `SourceBinDistributionGenerator` writes them, and this port already derives them -- the 80 bins and 125 distribution rows reproduce exactly. `opModePolProcAssoc`, `pollutantProcessAssoc` and `fuelType` are national tables that were simply not mounted; the first is now. `IMCoverage` is 2,024,874 national rows that narrow to ZERO for this county, so the emptiness the execution copy showed is a result here and not a premise.\n\nAND `soakActivityFraction` IS EMPTY NATIONALLY, which is the one place this document and MOVES do not agree on a row set. `TankTemperatureGenerator` writes it -- 2,645 lines of Java behind a quarter-hour tank-temperature recurrence -- and the default database ships all four of that generator's outputs with no rows. MOVES's own `opModeDistribution` for this run therefore has three rows where this port has one: 150 and 151 at value EXACTLY ZERO, and 300 at one. The emission is unaffected to the last bit, because at an on-network link `SourceHours` is `SHO` row for row, E1's ratio is exactly 1, and the soak weight `1 - fractionOfOperating` is exactly 0. THAT ZERO IS COMPUTED AND NOT ASSUMED. The document mounts the empty table, joins it on all five of its keys, and sums over no rows; the residual that gives mode 300 its weight is `greatest(0, 1 - SUM(soaking))` and not `fractionOfOperating`, which `docs/evap-leaks.md` §2.3 separates with a probe at 0.599999932 against 0.6. A document that wrote the soak weight as zero would agree here and be wrong at the first off-network link; one that wrote the residual as `fractionOfOperating` would be right to seven digits and wrong in general.\n\nAND THE ZERO IS LOAD-BEARING, which is measurable rather than arguable. The soaking modes are not weighted out because their rates are small: `emissionRateByAge` carries 2,188 rows at each of the three modes for `polProcessID` 113, and their mean `meanBaseRate` is 0.0989 g/h at Hot Soaking and 0.0514 at Cold Soaking against 0.9267 at All Running. Only the weight suppresses them. A document that gave the soaking modes any weight at all would be wrong by roughly a sixth, and `run_offNetworkLinkCount` -- which `tools/check-runspec-shape.py` asserts at 0 -- is what keeps the identity that makes the weight zero from becoming an assumption about the link.\n\nIT EMITS 64 ROWS: 41 gasoline model years and 23 E85 ones, at one county, one month and one day type. `n_outputRate` is 64 and the shape check recomputes it.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "evaporative"
    ]
  },
