        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspecroadtype": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/process-evap-leaks/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecroadtype.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecroadtype"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, roadTypeID 4, Urban Restricted Access -- an ON-NETWORK link, and that is what makes this run tractable. `TotalActivityGenerator` copies SHO into `SourceHours` row for row at an on-network link and takes it from SHP at the off-network one; `run_offNetworkLinkCount` asserts which arm this is, and E1's ratio is exactly 1 because of it.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspecsourcefueltype": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/process-evap-leaks/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecsourcefueltype.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecsourcefueltype"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope",
          "cohorts"
        ],
        "note": "4 rows: gasoline, diesel, E85 and electricity. Only gasoline and E85 reach the output, and by two routes that agree: `emissionRateByAge` carries `polProcessID` 113 for the 5,112 gasoline and 1,452 E85 bin-rows and for none of the diesel or electricity ones, and `fuelType.subjectToEvapCalculations` is `Y` on exactly those two. The second route is measurably inert here and the first does the work.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_movesoutput": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/process-evap-leaks/tables/db__out_process_evap_leaks__movesoutput.parquet"
      },
      "reader_options": {
        "float_columns": [
          "emissionQuant"
        ]
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "oracle",
          "expected-output"
        ],
        "note": "The 64-row expected output: 41 gasoline model years 1980-2020 and 23 E85 ones 1998-2020, all of pollutant 1 (THC) at process 13, totalling 760.305817 g. DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING -- reading it would transcribe the answer and its extent would transcribe the answer's shape. compare-output.py reads it directly under tolerance.toml.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspecpollutantprocess": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/process-evap-leaks/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecpollutantprocess.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecpollutantprocess"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "3 rows: 113 (THC x Evap Fuel Leaks), 8613 (TOG) and 8713 (VOC). ONLY 113 EMITS, and the reason is worth reading because it is not a filter anyone wrote: 8613 and 8713 are chained species -- `pollutantProcessAssoc` gives them `chainedTo1` 8013 and 7913 -- and `runspecchainedto` is EMPTY for this run, so MOVES computed no chain and neither table carries a rate for them. The port discards them through `rspp_hasRatedRow`, the same rule that makes a chained block as wide as its ratio table's coverage.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspecchainedto": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/process-evap-leaks/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecchainedto.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecchainedto"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope",
          "chain"
        ],
        "note": "ZERO rows, and it is the first document here where that is the interesting number. This run selects two chained pollutants and MOVES chained neither, so the edge list the port builds is the four declared CO2AE edges and nothing else -- none of which this run's pollutant-processes touch. A chain that fired on a declared edge without a selection behind it would show up here.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspeccounty": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/process-evap-leaks/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspeccounty.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspeccounty"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, countyID 26161 (Washtenaw, MI). It is the selection that makes the I/M lift empty: `IMCoverage` is 2,024,874 rows nationally and carries NO row for this county in any year, so L1's disaggregation produces nothing and the I/M blend is the identity -- measured from the national table rather than inherited from the execution copy's emptiness.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    }
  },
